        <body>
            <div xml:id="d180">

                <pb facs="0352" n="1006" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1006"/>

                <head>No. 479.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hunter to Mr. Gibbs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-09-14"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 14,
                        1875</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 11.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your dispatch No. 14, under
                    date of the 18th ultimo, relating to the death and funeral ceremonies of Rear-Ad
                    mind Napoleon Collins, U. S. N., I have to request that you will convey to the
                    Peruvian government the thanks of that of the United States for the signal
                    courtesies extended, and for the sympathy shown on the occasion.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. HUNTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
